      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test. The main issues with the original are the extremely verbose `new LevenshteinDistance(threshold).apply(SimilarityInputTest.build(cls, s1), SimilarityInputTest.build(cls, s2))` pattern repeated 30+ times, making it hard to see the actual test intent. I'll extract a helper method to reduce noise and make the assertions self-documenting.Now I'll compile-check the test.The improved test compiled successfully. The key change was extracting a `limitedDistance(cls, left, right, threshold)` helper method that eliminates the repeated `new LevenshteinDistance(threshold).apply(SimilarityInputTest.build(cls, ...), SimilarityInputTest.build(cls, ...))` boilerplate, making each assertion concise and letting the test values speak for themselves."
